1
00:01:29,160 --> 00:01:29,960
Da Ren

2
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:31,560
Time for New Year's Eve dinner.

3
00:01:32,080 --> 00:01:33,280
Digging in already?

4
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:34,240
Brother Ming

5
00:01:34,520 --> 00:01:35,960
Time flies so fast.

6
00:01:36,520 --> 00:01:37,560
It's the New Year again.

7
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:38,560
Tell me about it.

8
00:01:38,560 --> 00:01:39,360
Let me tell you,

9
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:40,360
during the New Year,

10
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:41,480
this is what I crave.

11
00:01:42,160 --> 00:01:43,120
Let me pour you a drink.

12
00:01:45,720 --> 00:01:46,520
Drink up.

13
00:01:47,840 --> 00:01:48,640
Da Ren

14
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:50,280
Is your leg any better?

15
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:51,560
Honestly,

16
00:01:51,960 --> 00:01:53,160
when the mine collapsed,

17
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:55,280
I didn't think I'd live to see the New Year.

18
00:01:55,640 --> 00:01:57,040
Don't talk nonsense.

19
00:01:58,280 --> 00:01:59,000
Let me tell you,

20
00:01:59,320 --> 00:02:00,840
you're too tough to die.

21
00:02:01,440 --> 00:02:03,040
Even the King of Hell wouldn't dare take you.

22
00:02:10,520 --> 00:02:11,280
Brother Ming

23
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:12,600
Thanks.

24
00:02:14,600 --> 00:02:15,440
If it weren't for you,

25
00:02:16,440 --> 00:02:18,160
I really would be dead.

26
00:02:18,720 --> 00:02:19,680
We

27
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:20,760
are brothers.

28
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:22,160
Brothers.

29
00:02:32,280 --> 00:02:33,680
My mom wrote me a letter.

30
00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:35,840
She said

31
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:37,800
her old illness is acting up again.

32
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:42,880
Deep down,

33
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:44,880
I feel terrible.

34
00:02:45,440 --> 00:02:46,360
You know,

35
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:47,320
you just focus on healing.

36
00:02:48,080 --> 00:02:49,280
And once you're recovered,

37
00:02:49,280 --> 00:02:50,520
go back to see her soon.

38
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:51,720
If you're short on cash,

39
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:53,400
just tell me.

40
00:02:58,080 --> 00:02:58,880
As for us,

41
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:00,840
we're coal miners.

42
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:03,840
Spending all day down in this mine,

43
00:03:03,840 --> 00:03:05,040
never seeing the light of day.

44
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:07,520
But sometimes, when I think about it...

45
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:09,800
how the black coal we dig up

46
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:12,080
can give our parents a good life,

47
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:14,400
let me tell you, this work

48
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:15,400
just gets me fired up.

49
00:03:16,360 --> 00:03:17,160
Brother Ming,

50
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:19,240
no matter what happens,

51
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:21,320
your business is my business.

52
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:23,280
Your family is my family.

53
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:24,760
Alright.

54
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:32,200
Come on.

55
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:32,520
Da Ren,

56
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:36,720
Happy New Year.

57
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:39,480
Brother Ming, I can't accept this.

58
00:03:39,480 --> 00:03:40,200
Take it.

59
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:41,200
It's the New Year.

60
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:42,240
It's for good luck.

61
00:03:42,240 --> 00:03:43,160
Just take it.

62
00:03:51,160 --> 00:03:54,080
This bite means surplus year after year.

63
00:03:57,280 --> 00:03:58,360
Go on, take it.

64
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:18,600
Da Ren

65
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:21,960
Happy New Year!

66
00:04:22,880 --> 00:04:24,200
Happy New Year, Brother Ming!

67
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:29,080
Stop!

68
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:32,880
Stop!

69
00:04:35,440 --> 00:04:36,320
Stop!

70
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:40,320
Stop!

71
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:41,560
Hurry! This way! Hurry, hurry!

72
00:04:49,880 --> 00:04:51,600
You're dead if I catch you!

73
00:04:53,720 --> 00:04:54,320
Hurry, hurry, hurry!

74
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:54,920
Hurry!

75
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:01,120
You're dead if I catch you!

76
00:05:01,400 --> 00:05:01,960
Stop right there!

77
00:05:14,280 --> 00:05:14,680
Don't run!

78
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:16,560
Stop right there! Stop!

79
00:05:16,960 --> 00:05:17,600
Stop!

80
00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:19,040
You better not let me catch you!

81
00:05:21,720 --> 00:05:23,080
If I catch you, I'll break your legs!

82
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:24,080
Over there! Hurry!

83
00:05:24,080 --> 00:05:24,640
Freeze!

84
00:05:25,240 --> 00:05:26,160
Over there!

85
00:05:26,880 --> 00:05:27,640
Get them!

86
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:29,120
They ran this way!

87
00:05:36,320 --> 00:05:37,760
I can't keep going, Chen Baixi.

88
00:05:38,920 --> 00:05:40,080
I feel a bit sick.

89
00:05:40,520 --> 00:05:41,520
I think it's low blood sugar.

90
00:06:05,120 --> 00:06:05,960
They're here!

91
00:06:06,560 --> 00:06:07,720
They're in this alley!

92
00:06:08,360 --> 00:06:08,920
Hurry!

93
00:06:43,280 --> 00:06:43,840
Hurry, hurry!

94
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:44,960
Almost there.

95
00:06:47,640 --> 00:06:48,480
We're back.

96
00:06:49,960 --> 00:06:50,640
You two...

97
00:06:51,200 --> 00:06:52,680
are you eloping?

98
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:56,680
No, no.

99
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:57,720
We were just...

100
00:06:57,720 --> 00:06:59,720
at Prosperity Funeral Home.

101
00:07:00,480 --> 00:07:01,040
Right.

102
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:01,840
And got recognized.

103
00:07:03,520 --> 00:07:07,600
I heard Prosperity's business is booming.

104
00:07:07,840 --> 00:07:09,920
Did you find out what's going on?

105
00:07:10,200 --> 00:07:12,440
To sum it up briefly:

106
00:07:12,440 --> 00:07:13,520
selling shoddy goods,

107
00:07:13,760 --> 00:07:15,040
profiting off filial piety,

108
00:07:15,040 --> 00:07:16,360
emotional blackmail,

109
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:17,240
and excessive marketing.

110
00:07:18,520 --> 00:07:20,640
They're making a fortune off the dead.

111
00:07:20,920 --> 00:07:22,640
Aren't they afraid of being struck by lightning?

112
00:07:23,160 --> 00:07:25,560
As good rises, evil rises higher.

113
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:26,640
Xiaofang,

114
00:07:26,640 --> 00:07:28,560
you're quite obsessed with money yourself,

115
00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:30,440
but compared to them,

116
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:32,840
you're just an amateur.

117
00:07:34,920 --> 00:07:36,360
I've heard people say

118
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:39,640
they even make 3/4 sleeve burial clothes.

119
00:07:40,520 --> 00:07:41,640
Shroud exposing hands,

120
00:07:41,640 --> 00:07:43,160
descendants begging for food.

121
00:07:43,400 --> 00:07:44,280
I think they really

122
00:07:44,280 --> 00:07:46,000
have no professional ethics at all.

123
00:07:47,040 --> 00:07:49,360
How shameless they truly are.

124
00:07:52,040 --> 00:07:52,520
Dad,

125
00:07:53,080 --> 00:07:55,400
weren't you jealous of their good business?

126
00:07:55,400 --> 00:07:56,760
You even told us to reflect.

127
00:07:57,600 --> 00:08:00,160
Why don't we learn to diversify like them?

128
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:03,120
Nonsense!

129
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:05,120
The rules set by our ancestors

130
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:06,560
demand a bottom line.

131
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:12,560
If you sell out your conscience here...

132
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:17,040
We must be decent people.

133
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:18,600
Excuse me.

134
00:08:18,720 --> 00:08:19,400
Sorry to interrupt.

135
00:08:19,400 --> 00:08:20,080
I'm looking for...

136
00:08:21,040 --> 00:08:21,840
Ms. Li.

137
00:08:22,600 --> 00:08:23,960
I need your help.

138
00:08:31,640 --> 00:08:32,840
You two,

139
00:08:32,840 --> 00:08:34,600
that's roughly our family's situation.

140
00:08:45,640 --> 00:08:47,320
My late father-in-law had diabetes.

141
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:49,440
He had trouble getting around lately.

142
00:08:49,440 --> 00:08:51,880
He'd sit by this window to get some sun.

143
00:08:54,040 --> 00:08:55,040
You've got some nerve.

144
00:08:55,720 --> 00:08:57,960
So you're calling the shots here now, huh?

145
00:08:58,760 --> 00:08:59,760
All of you, get out right now!

146
00:09:02,040 --> 00:09:02,560
I'm sorry.

147
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:06,240
Excuse me.

148
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:08,600
Our employer is your wife.

149
00:09:08,600 --> 00:09:10,640
We only follow our employer's wishes.

150
00:09:13,360 --> 00:09:14,040
Get out! Get out! Get out!

151
00:09:14,040 --> 00:09:14,640
Get out!

152
00:09:15,080 --> 00:09:15,760
You...

153
00:09:15,800 --> 00:09:17,520
I still call the shots in this house!

154
00:09:18,080 --> 00:09:19,400
I already signed a contract with them.

155
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:20,440
And I paid the deposit.

156
00:09:20,440 --> 00:09:22,560
Dad's funeral must be respectable.

157
00:09:22,840 --> 00:09:24,240
I just want to give our dad

158
00:09:24,440 --> 00:09:26,320
a great funeral! What's wrong with that?

159
00:09:34,200 --> 00:09:35,200
When he was alive,

160
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:36,160
how many times did you take care of him?

161
00:09:37,040 --> 00:09:38,040
Now that he's gone,

162
00:09:38,040 --> 00:09:39,480
suddenly you care about appearances?

163
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:40,640
What do you mean I didn't care for him?

164
00:09:40,640 --> 00:09:41,800
That's my dad!

165
00:09:45,360 --> 00:09:46,960
Then do you know where

166
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:48,800
to inject his insulin?

167
00:09:49,560 --> 00:09:50,840
This is our family business.

168
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:51,840
Why are you butting in?

169
00:09:54,160 --> 00:09:55,280
Then tell me!

170
00:09:56,560 --> 00:09:56,880
It's...

171
00:09:56,880 --> 00:09:58,040
just in the arm, right?

172
00:09:58,040 --> 00:09:58,720
His arm.

173
00:09:58,720 --> 00:09:59,680
Where else would it be?

174
00:10:00,680 --> 00:10:02,040
Ms. Zhao, do you know?

175
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:05,600
Outer upper arm, a quarter way down.

176
00:10:05,880 --> 00:10:07,960
Five centimeters around the navel.

177
00:10:07,960 --> 00:10:09,120
And the outer thighs.

178
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:10,480
You have to rotate the injection sites.

179
00:10:11,040 --> 00:10:13,400
This ensures the meds are absorbed

180
00:10:13,400 --> 00:10:14,520
and reduces complications.

181
00:10:15,160 --> 00:10:16,440
What does that prove?

182
00:10:19,160 --> 00:10:20,000
Mr. Wang,

183
00:10:20,640 --> 00:10:22,440
this is your late father's diary.

184
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:52,120
That darn old man.

185
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:54,720
So he remembered everything after all.

186
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:05,000
This shows that

187
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:07,360
Ms. Zhao has treated your father

188
00:11:08,080 --> 00:11:09,480
like her own flesh and blood.

189
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:16,000
I wanted to spend a fortune on his funeral

190
00:11:16,560 --> 00:11:18,160
just to be a dutiful son, didn't I?

191
00:11:19,800 --> 00:11:21,560
A glass of water by the bedside in life

192
00:11:22,080 --> 00:11:23,680
is worth more than tons of ashes at the grave

193
00:11:27,440 --> 00:11:28,360
Mr. Wang,

194
00:11:29,360 --> 00:11:30,520
your father's biggest regret

195
00:11:30,520 --> 00:11:32,360
was not giving you a proper education.

196
00:11:34,280 --> 00:11:35,920
I believe he'd want you to spend the money

197
00:11:35,920 --> 00:11:37,520
on your child's education.

198
00:11:38,520 --> 00:11:40,640
He wouldn't want you to share his regret.

199
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:49,240
Ms. Zhao,

200
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:53,280
we understand your needs now.

201
00:11:54,080 --> 00:11:54,960
You can just ask Prosperity

202
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:56,720
to follow this more economical plan.

203
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:04,160
Thank you, Ms. Li.

204
00:12:05,120 --> 00:12:06,240
How much do I owe you?

205
00:12:08,640 --> 00:12:10,360
We don't charge for consultations.

206
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:16,800
Goodbye.

207
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:21,320
Thank you.

208
00:12:43,280 --> 00:12:44,680
Do you guys remember?

209
00:12:45,840 --> 00:12:47,640
Standing right here back then,

210
00:12:47,640 --> 00:12:50,080
I said I was leaving Lecang,

211
00:12:50,080 --> 00:12:51,320
and never coming back.

212
00:12:52,080 --> 00:12:53,640
Never thought I'd end up coming back.

213
00:12:55,840 --> 00:12:58,280
I thought if I got into acting school,

214
00:12:58,280 --> 00:13:00,000
I'd definitely make it big.

215
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:02,960
But reality dragged me through the mud.

216
00:13:02,960 --> 00:13:05,720
This is what you call Life's boomerang.

217
00:13:05,920 --> 00:13:08,440
Hitting you right between the eyes later.

218
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:15,600
As kids, we thought we had control,

219
00:13:16,400 --> 00:13:18,200
only to go around in circles and realize

220
00:13:19,080 --> 00:13:20,480
we're right back where we started.

221
00:13:20,720 --> 00:13:21,920
Yiran.

222
00:13:21,920 --> 00:13:23,280
There's no turning back now.

223
00:13:23,520 --> 00:13:24,680
You're not allowed to regret this.

224
00:13:26,280 --> 00:13:27,640
Don't worry.

225
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:29,000
The decisions I make,

226
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:30,240
I never regret.

227
00:13:30,880 --> 00:13:32,000
What's there to regret?

228
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:33,440
Time to eat!

229
00:13:34,080 --> 00:13:34,880
Let's eat, let's eat.

230
00:13:36,160 --> 00:13:37,080
Let's eat, let's eat.

231
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:38,320
Mr. Chen.

232
00:13:38,320 --> 00:13:39,920
Drinking by yourself already?

233
00:13:40,680 --> 00:13:41,080
Come on.

234
00:13:41,080 --> 00:13:41,640
Xiaofang.

235
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:43,000
Thanks, Auntie Lan.

236
00:13:43,480 --> 00:13:44,520
Thanks, Auntie Lan.

237
00:13:44,680 --> 00:13:45,280
Here.

238
00:13:46,080 --> 00:13:46,880
Hurry up.

239
00:13:47,680 --> 00:13:48,480
Here's one for you.

240
00:13:48,480 --> 00:13:49,200
Thanks.

241
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:50,960
Have one, Xiaofang.

242
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:51,800
Smells so good.

243
00:13:54,440 --> 00:13:55,600
Stop chewing your chopsticks.

244
00:13:55,600 --> 00:13:56,600
Eat up.

245
00:13:57,160 --> 00:13:58,680
Thinking about that couple today...

246
00:13:58,680 --> 00:13:59,800
makes me lose my appetite.

247
00:14:00,200 --> 00:14:01,320
Did they bully you?

248
00:14:01,600 --> 00:14:03,600
They were forced by a shady funeral home

249
00:14:03,600 --> 00:14:04,880
into emotional blackmail.

250
00:14:04,920 --> 00:14:06,080
Living beyond their means,

251
00:14:06,080 --> 00:14:08,120
insisting on an expensive funeral.

252
00:14:10,720 --> 00:14:12,120
But it's true that nowadays,

253
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:14,160
funerals are so expensive.

254
00:14:14,640 --> 00:14:16,680
Remember my professional mourning gig?

255
00:14:17,040 --> 00:14:18,480
Eight hundred bucks a pop just to cry.

256
00:14:19,040 --> 00:14:21,080
If I kick the bucket in the future,

257
00:14:21,080 --> 00:14:22,360
please don't make a big fuss for me.

258
00:14:22,360 --> 00:14:23,520
And don't hire professional mourners.

259
00:14:23,520 --> 00:14:25,520
Just bury me with your Pops.

260
00:14:25,520 --> 00:14:26,320
Wu Huilian!

261
00:14:26,400 --> 00:14:28,280
Can you stop talking about dying all day?

262
00:14:29,400 --> 00:14:30,480
I'm talking about the future!

263
00:14:30,480 --> 00:14:31,640
I didn't say right now.

264
00:14:31,800 --> 00:14:32,280
Ptoo, ptoo, ptoo.

265
00:14:32,280 --> 00:14:33,080
Knock on wood, quick!

266
00:14:33,240 --> 00:14:33,520
Right.

267
00:14:33,520 --> 00:14:34,200
Knock on wood.

268
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:36,320
Ptoo, ptoo, ptoo.

269
00:14:36,960 --> 00:14:37,680
Here.

270
00:14:38,680 --> 00:14:39,480
Thanks.

271
00:14:40,440 --> 00:14:41,440
I got it!

272
00:14:43,200 --> 00:14:44,880
Have you guys heard of Green Burial?

273
00:14:46,080 --> 00:14:47,080
I know it.

274
00:14:47,080 --> 00:14:48,080
It's what big cities

275
00:14:48,080 --> 00:14:50,960
are doing, like flower or tree burials.

276
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:51,800
Yes, exactly.

277
00:14:51,840 --> 00:14:53,440
What the heck is a flower bed burial?

278
00:14:53,840 --> 00:14:54,600
It means

279
00:14:54,600 --> 00:14:57,280
putting the ashes in a biodegradable urn

280
00:14:57,280 --> 00:14:59,120
and burying it by flowers or a tree.

281
00:14:59,120 --> 00:14:59,880
This way,

282
00:14:59,880 --> 00:15:01,480
it's cheaper than a regular cemetery,

283
00:15:01,480 --> 00:15:02,600
and it's also very eco-friendly.

284
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:04,560
First time I've heard of that.

285
00:15:04,640 --> 00:15:05,560
Me too.

286
00:15:05,560 --> 00:15:06,200
Really?

287
00:15:06,200 --> 00:15:06,600
Come on.

288
00:15:06,600 --> 00:15:07,520
Let's have a drink, just us two.

289
00:15:07,520 --> 00:15:07,680
Sure.

290
00:15:07,680 --> 00:15:09,000
Since it's a first for both of us.

291
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:09,680
Okay, Auntie Lan.

292
00:15:09,800 --> 00:15:10,240
Cheers.

293
